  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two ions of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>amu</mi></math>&nbsp; and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>amu</mi></math>&nbsp;have charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> respectively. These ions pass through the region of the constant perpendicular magnetic field. The kinetic energy of both ions is the same. Then:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "lighter ion will be deflected less than heavier ion",
      "is_correct": false
    },
