    {
      "text": "no ion will be deflected",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The relation between linear moment and radius in terms of the magnitude of magnetic field and charge of a particle,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mi>q</mi></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.</p>"
